<article class="env-lemma" id="0H79">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0H79">Lemma <span data-tag="0H79">17.28.14</span>.</a> Let $f : X \to Y$, $g : Y \to S$ be morphisms of ringed spaces Then there is a canonical exact sequence </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  f^*\Omega _{Y/S} \to \Omega _{X/S} \to \Omega _{X/Y} \to 0  \]
</div>
  <p> where the maps come from applications of Lemma <a href="/tag/08RU" data-tag="08RU">17.28.12</a>. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      By taking induced maps in stalks at $x \in X$ and using Lemma <a href="/tag/08TE" data-tag="08TE">17.28.7</a> we obtain a sequence 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  \mathcal{O}_{X, x} \otimes _{\mathcal{O}_{Y, f(x)}} \Omega _{\mathcal{O}_{Y, f(x)}/\mathcal{O}_{S, g(f(x))}} \to \Omega _{\mathcal{O}_{X, x}/\mathcal{O}_{S, g(f(x))}} \to \Omega _{\mathcal{O}_{X, x}/\mathcal{O}_{Y, f(x)}} \to 0  \]
</div>
    <p>
       It suffices to see that the maps of the sequence are the same as the ones in Algebra, Lemma <a href="/tag/00RS" data-tag="00RS">10.131.7</a>. This is because the characterization of the maps in Lemma <a href="/tag/08RU" data-tag="08RU">17.28.12</a> and because via the isomorphism of Sheaves, Lemma <a href="/tag/0098" data-tag="0098">6.26.4</a> we have $(f^*s)_ x = s_ x \otimes 1$, for any local section $s$ of a sheaf of $\mathcal{O}_ Y$-modules. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>